Files: src/dirmult.c R/dirmult_ttest.r src/dirmult_lm.c R/dirmult_lm.r
Copyright: 2026 ALDEx3 authors
Comment: dirmult_lm() (src/dirmult_lm.c, R/dirmult_lm.r) is a C port of the
 linear-model path of aldex() from ALDEx3 1.4.0, restructured for ecodive:
 aldex() and aldex.sampler() (R/aldex.R, R/aldex-internals.R: Dirichlet
 draws plus a scale model, per Monte Carlo draw), rLogDirichlet()
 (R/dirichlet.R), the scale models clr.sm(), tss.sm() and sample.sm()
 (R/scale.R), fflm() (R/fflm.R: least squares with classical, HC0 and HC3
 standard errors and one-sided t tail probabilities), aldex.pvals()
 (R/aldex-internals.R: the averaging of the draws' doubled one-sided
 p-values, raw and adjusted) and summary.aldex() (R/aldex-summary.R).
 The scale model of dirmult_ttest() (scale_sd) follows clr.sm() from
 ALDEx3 1.4.0 (R/scale.R): one N(0, scale_sd^2) log2 shift per Monte Carlo
 draw for each coefficient of the design, here the treatment-versus-reference
 indicator of the contrast (the intercept's shift cancels from every
 difference). Its pooled_sd and effect columns follow aldex.effect() and
 .aldex_pooled_var() from ALDEx3 1.4.0 (R/aldex-summary.R): the mean over
 the draws of the pooled within-group standard deviation, and of the
 contrast's coefficient divided by it (cohens.d). The rest of these files is
 under the scikit-bio license above or Copyright 2026 ecodive authors, under
 the MIT license above.
