 How these files differ from the originals (Artistic License 2.0, section 4):
 they are a modified version, restructured for ecodive. The lm() fits of the
 frequency test are replaced by their residual sums of squares and the
 prevalence test's tables by per-batch presence counts, computed in one
 threaded C pass over a sparse table (src/decontam.c); prop.test() and
 fisher.test() are replaced by their formulas, vectorized over features in
